Algonex Industry Scenario: Imagine you work as a Junior Data Analyst / SQL Developer for an e-commerce company

The business wants to analyze:
- customer purchases
product sales
- employee/salesperson performance
daily revenue
- customer spending
rankings
- growth
repeat purchases
- top products
moving averages
- percentile/segment analysis -> We will build one table and solve all of these with MySQL window functions

  -- Create the Database
CREATE DATABASE ecommerce_analytics;
USE ecommerce_analytics;

--3. Create the Main Table
We'll create an orders table
CREATE TABLE orders (
    order_id INT PRIMARY KEY, -- Unique order
    order_date DATE NOT NULL, -- Date of purchase
    customer_id INT NOT NULL, -- Customer identifier
    customer_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL, -- Customer name
    city VARCHAR(50),                    -- Customer city
    product_name VARCHAR(100),           -- Product purchased
    category VARCHAR(50),                -- Product category
    quantity INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,      -- Number of units
    unit_price DECIMAL(10,2) NOT NULL,  -- Price per unit
    sales_rep VARCHAR(100),              -- Employee handling sale
    payment_method VARCHAR(30)         -- Payment type
);

